From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:22:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Horizon on Linux: constant buffer 1 holds the shader's
 constants, textures are read again when the game writes them

39% of Xenoblade Chronicles 2's shaders (1502 of 3867) read constant buffer 1, which the driver fills
with the constant segment of the shader's code area (control +0x700..+0x704, or what follows part B of
a vertex shader in two parts). It was zeros, so characters and scenery came out as black silhouettes.
A texture was read from memory only at its first use; the game streams texture data in later. aot_hash64
(a hash of guest memory, sampled for big textures) is compared once a frame and the texture is read
again when it changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux S7bis: shader constant buffer 1 and textures written after first use
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

